{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians","id":1410146,"title":"Destroyed Antediluvians","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-24T15:53:28-07:00","id":1410146,"title":"Destroyed Antediluvians","content":"There are only two Antediluvians who were really destroyed, Ilyes and Zapathasura. In both cases their clans (True Brujah and Ravnos respectively) were reduced to a handful of members after their founders met Final Death. This also supports the theory that Veddartha was not really destroyed despite what the Ventrue clan elders think.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T15:58:58-07:00","id":1410147,"title":"","content":"That makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:13:32-07:00","id":1410148,"title":"","content":"Set is, as far as the Followers of Set and Werewolves are concerned, also permanently dead. The Followers of Set are just researching a way to bring him back.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I like the theory that &quot;True Brujah&quot; was Ventrue and Troile is the father of the Brujah clan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:35:24-07:00","id":1410151,"title":"","content":"It is my personal belief that Antediluvians can't be destroyed, save for Diablerie where the power is passed along to another vampire maybe even under the control of the Antediluvian, and that any story involving the destruction of an Antediluvian is a myth or misunderstanding of some kind. Of course, this isn't canon, but it's how I think of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T16:48:12-07:00","id":1410155,"title":"","content":"The Trujah stories might not be true, though, and perhaps they're really the offshoot and the regular Brujah really are the originals. I'm not saying they aren't true, just that they might not be. It's a little hard to believe somebody who could literally see the future, travel back with that knowledge and stop time would have been killed. Unless that's just what he wanted everyone to think.<br /> <br /> I agree that signs point to Ventrue surviving a lot longer than the fall of the second city, just because there were 4th Gens embraced later, like Alexander. Although it's entirely possible they diablerized their way down to 4th.<br /> <br /> What about Cappadocius/Ashur? Giovanni offed him back around the Renaissance. Everyone seems to agree that was a good thing.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T18:30:43-07:00","id":1410175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410155#post1410155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Trujah stories might not be true, though, and perhaps they're really the offshoot and the regular Brujah really are the originals.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think somewhere they mentioned Brujah only had Troile as a descendant. Which would mean both were true.<br /> <br /> Besides, regular Brujah are STILL descendants of Brujah as he's Troile's sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:01:13-07:00","id":1410180,"title":"","content":"There are Antediluvians who have died, and one that may (or may not) exist but have been removed from the playing field. These include; Ravnos, Brujah/Troile, Cappadocius, Ventrue, and Set.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410148#post1410148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, I like the theory that &quot;True Brujah&quot; was Ventrue and Troile is the father of the Brujah clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I heard that before, but it has possibilities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1208,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","user":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","date":". 08-24-2020, 10:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T19:07:05-07:00","id":1410182,"title":"","content":"I liked the idea of [Brujah] being destroyed since it happened way before Antediluvian reached the godlike powers the Cainites fear in the last 3 or 4 millennia. There's a very thin line between slight time manipulation at higher Temporis powers and actual time travel (which would be very anticlimatic when it comes to storytell vampires), therefore, I believe the possibility of [Brujah] being restored can only be through mystical restoration, not actual TARDIS time travelling.<br /> <br /> Dracian (Zapathasura) fight against the bodhisattvas and his following destruction was a really great addition to the metaplot. I like him being dead.<br /> <br /> On Set, he is MIA. After his disappearance in Ombos during the time of the crucifiction, nobody knows what actually happened to him. I like this story seed since it w as never defined if he was destroyed or went into hiding (what would Set hide from?).<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the diablerie of Cappadocius by Augustus, it was a very detailed scenario (GC1) that can be polished with current lore on the Cappadocian clan and the elders it featured to become a more accurate characterization than it was back then.<br /> <br /> I heavily disliked the &quot;dead a long time ago&quot; of [Ventrue], and also disliked the [Ventrue] and Veddartha being two separate beings only because of the misinterpretation that began with the stats of TC2 in both Maltheas (who is 4th) and Hardestadt (who is 6th) and nobody understood. Both hypothesis I dislike exist due to this and after being discussed for SOOOO long in the old forums, it kinda stuck (I lie told often enough becomes truth -Lenin).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T20:07:53-07:00","id":1410199,"title":"","content":"Originally, this was a cool mystery and I was interested in a canonical answer. However, all the various retcons and other changes through the various editions have left me cold to any &quot;official&quot; answer. Because the official answer keeps changing based on the the whim of the current developer.<br /> <br /> At this point, I'm only interested as much as this is issue is important to any specific ST and whether it's important to that specific chronicle. For 99+% of chronicles, it's a non-issue as it does not affect anything at all in the chronicle or greater setting. For example, I don't think most STs really give this any thought or develop their setting differently in any way based on whether or not that antedeluvian or this one is truly dead. There's no actual Jyhad playing out in their games.<br /> <br /> This isn't a criticism of those games. It would require a lot more effort to figure out a Jyhad style chronicle (with multiple layers of mystery, and secret plots hatching out) than a normal chronicle. And very often for little payout. I must admit I rarely take the time to do this with my own chronicles. As such, I think almost any decision by the ST could be interesting based on how it plays out in game.<br /> <br /> For my own chronicles, I decided on the following lore. But whether these actually have any impact in how I run my own games, I don't know. It'd be subtle if it was, as I'm not intentionally making decisions based on them.<br /> <br /> First, I have that Ventrue is truly dead because I like the idea the clan is free of antedeluvian machinations. I think one reason I've become so wedded to this is while this was something I picked up right away when I first read the second edition corebook way back in 1992, I can honestly say that none of the players I've had in my game ever knew this. They read right over it. (And of course once I mention this as part of some chronicle background prep, as part of roleplay, the player always makes a comment that this can't possibly be true because it would be such a convenient story if the antedeluvian is alive.) It seems this is something many posters here have debated online for a while, but in my experience most players don't realize this is an old canonical point. Veddartha is not the name of the founder, but his childer and Mithras diablerized someone to become 4th generation.<br /> <br /> Second, Cappadocious is dead, but he wasn't successfully diablerized because Augustus botched it. Cappadocious knew some serious lore about death, and this was all part of a plan. The classic &quot;sacrifice yourself for greater knowledge&quot; ploy. But if he survived somehow in the Underworld to continue on with his plans, he isn't coming back as a vampire. Very strong possibility he still plays a role in starting Gehenna/the Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> Third, I never liked the True Brujah idea or Temporis. But I'm on the fence whether to keep the idea that Troile killed Ilyes and usurped the clan. It makes much thematic sense. So I'm leaning that Brujah is dead with Troile being the only childer of Ilyes that every other Brujah is descended from.<br /> <br /> Fourth, Set is destroyed. Jesus destroyed him during his forty days in the desert when Set tried to tempt him. This doesn't actually fit the known fact of Set's disappearance in AD 33 (since it occurred in the beginning of Jesus' ministry not at the end of his life), but it's close enough. The Setites still think they can somehow return Set back to existence though (and only the top most circle of the Set cult knows the details of Set's destruction, it is a closely kept secret).<br /> <br /> Fifth, while Lasombra was not diablerized, his use of Obtenebration sucked him into the Abyss never to return. Don't know if that counts as dead or not, but for all practical purposes he's gone.<br /> <br /> Toreador, Malkavian, Nosferatu, Tzimisce, and Salubri (in the weird way he is in Tremere) are definitely still around. The others are uncertain as I haven't decided anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-24T20:10:43-07:00","id":1410202,"title":"","content":"My point was that details on Brujah might be muddier than they seem and it's hard to be sure, just like with Ventrue, because it supposedly happened so long ago. The V20 Lore of the Clans book gives some alternatives. One of them is that Ventrue diablerized Brujah and Troile in turn diablerized Ventrue. Another was that Troile was the real antedeluvian and Brujah was the usurper. It doesn't say for sure which is right.<br /> <br /> I hate to wonder if it might be some horrible paradox where Brujah and Troile are the same person from different times and they diablerized themself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T07:54:48-07:00","id":1410291,"title":"","content":"I know Gehenna is not canon, but I still think the section before the scenarios is interesting. The bit with the Spoiler Warning: This is the &quot;official&quot; status of the members of the Third Generation that WW kept track of and had notes on.<br /> <br /> It lists Brujah, Set, Lasombra, Ravnos, and Ventrue as having met final death.<br /> <br /> I think the most likely culprit for Set is Osiris. He had been building power for millennia, specifically vanished from Duat at the time, and hated Set since they were mortal brothers. Motive, means, opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-25-2020, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:09:51-07:00","id":1410295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians#post1410146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only two Antediluvians who were really destroyed, Ilyes and Zapathasura. In both cases their clans (True Brujah and Ravnos respectively) were reduced to a handful of members after their founders met Final Death. This also supports the theory that Veddartha was not really destroyed despite what the Ventrue clan elders think.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That assertion depends on the matter of one taking the Temporis bloodline's claim of being the direct, pure descendants of Ilyes as actual truth in the first place, in fact. And apparently many posters have said essentially the same in different words. Oh well, it happens.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the matter of Antediluvians existing, destroyed or not and etc can be something of a quite slippery slope, as truth be told what separates mechanically a clan of a bloodline. What evidence does one have beside hearsay and a sufficiently puisant kindred with the right discipline set?<br /> <br /> What happens if a 5th or 4th gen of decides to learn some bloodline's signature discipline and develop it to levels beyond anyone else's ken?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 03-08-2023, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:13:30-07:00","id":1410297,"title":"","content":"Wait what was up with Veddartha and Ventrue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:28:52-07:00","id":1410302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410297#post1410297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what was up with Veddartha and Ventrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their Facebook status is &quot;Its complicated.&quot;<br /> <br /> Ok, the short version is that Veddartha has been listed as the sire of both Mithras (4th generation) and the sire of Maltheas (5th generation). So the assumption was that Mithras comitted diablerie. However a later book listed Mithras sire as &quot;The Ventrue Antediluvian&quot;<br /> <br /> So theories are that Veddartha, meaning &quot;Wise one&quot; is an archaic title for the eldest Ventrue or some sort of title. Or that the original Veddartha met final death, and the Ventrue or a Ventrue covered it up. So there were a 4rth generation kindred assumed the name and mantle of the Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> This fits the tales of the Ventrue Antediluvian being destroyed, and Maltheas being sire almost two thousand years later than Mithras.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-25-2020, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T08:52:56-07:00","id":1410305,"title":"","content":"I just use Veddartha as the Ventrue Ante and ignore the part about Maltheas. I barely even know who Maltheas is lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T09:03:07-07:00","id":1410308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410305#post1410305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just use Veddartha as the Ventrue Ante and ignore the part about Maltheas. I barely even know who Maltheas is lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maltheas is some &quot;you blink &amp; you miss it&quot; Inconnu methuselah playing much younger vampire in the Council of Thorns in Transylvania Chronicles II, if memory tricks me not. More relevant for the implications he brings about Mithras than anything, truth be told.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of taste actually. Personally there's something that i find deeply entertaining in the idea of Mithras' claim to be a childe of the Ventrue Antediluvian being as much of a lie as that of being the persian sun god. Because let's be honest, <i>how many kindred around actually have the knowledge, power and desire to challenge or prove him wrong anyway</i>? The guy was <b><i>already </i></b>a methuselah when Sejanus/Vitel was embraced, back in the early decades of the Roman Empire! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But speaking of Antediluvians, another thing that i have done in my games overall is break from the clan-antediluvian corelation, with bits and pieces here and there implying much of the lore is imprecise or intentionally false. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Like, the lion's share of noddism as we know it is based on fabrications from late roman to medieval era by the Cappadocians, for the sake of selling their pro-christianism take of the kindred condition and origins and consolidate their (false) claims of being an actual clan, instead of the rejected remnants that they were of the Salubri developed before Saulot's legendary journey to the East.</i><br /> <br /> <i>And no, the Giovanni are <b>not </b>their descendants - in fact, they are closer to the Lasombra, both groups being just cabals that usurped the same original clan in the chaos of the late medieval Italian Peninsula and are now to this day alternately bragging or cursing each other over who actually diablerized their Ante, when they do admit it was the same Ante and one of the sides is lying, that is. But i digress. Anyway, the Caps' extinction owes more to their own religious manias, cults and peculiar discipline making them prime target for medieval &amp; renaissance era. That said, the Giovanni sure misdirected church officials - and stole their loot from church vaults - more than any other group of kindred.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Is Baba Yaga the Grandmother of all Nosferatu or a Niktuku? Let me ask you another question instead. If those Sabbat knuckleheads were able to find a way to break apart the blood bond, why would millenia-old kindred embraced <b>for their sheer unadulterated viciousness</b> still be loyal and focused on their sire's dictates after so long?</i><br /> <br /> <i>The Baali are no clan or bloodline. They are what happens when Caitiffs are haunted by the shade of an Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> Want to know what an Antediluvian is like? Go to Gary, ask Lucian for the truth.<br /> <br /> The Tremere's whole story is a lie - oh, don't get me wrong, they believe every bit of it is truth, but honestly? They are being tricked. There has always been a clan of blood, messing with the qualities of vitae. It may change names, origin and character, but there's always one such clan of so-called magicians. My sire suspects all of them are works in progress of some Antediluvian that changes identities and cleans the slate when it gets bored.<br /> The Salubri might be their precursors - or their sucessors - depending on when you ask my sire on the subject.<br /> <br /> There is no 2nd generation - or 1st generation for that matter, but i digress. There's only the Antediluvians, that might - or not - have a common origin and those under him. In fact i've heard stories that the Antes were just like what we call 4th gens, but then ascended into something more through mastery of their souls and the disciplines of the blood. Golconda might or not be a form of this,in fact. The real matter is that as being an Ante is a matter of enlightnement/transcedence, not just blood, diablerie always fail, because by blood they are &quot;just&quot; another 4th gen.</i> </div> </div> </div>Among a bunch of other stuff i've thrown as &quot;lore monkeywrench&quot; in my chronicles. When i don't do worse, like the &quot;Lucian is THE Lucian&quot; or thrown some apocryphal antediluvian like i did in my rewrite of the gonzo adventure in Berlin By Night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-25-2020, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T09:07:25-07:00","id":1410309,"title":"","content":"I think whether they're alive or not is kept vague so the storyteller can surprise the players; Did Ventrue die a long time ago, or is he sleeping under the BBC headquarters awaiting the time to rise and control the world? Did Set fake his death, can he be resurrected, are his followers trying to manifest him as a spirit, or are they wasting their time over a corpse? <br /> <br /> Ravnos actually being dead is pretty silly given his main shtick is creating epic illusions. <br /> <br /> By 2020<br /> Capadocious- Playing Wraith<br /> Giovanni- Dead. <br /> Lasombra-Alive. Fun idea; He was montano all along. <br /> Set- Lost<br /> Nos- Alive, and he's coming for you. <br /> Troil-gonna fight the power any time now... <br /> <br /> Other ideas: <br /> The Antes became human again. <br /> The Antes got bored and killed themselves<br /> The Antes are all sleeping.<br /> The Antes are all disembodied; Tsmisce is a disease, Malkav is a mental illness, Lasombra is the Abyss itself. Saulot became a demon, Set became Umbrood... <br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly I keep em well away from my players so it makes no difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:16:12-07:00","id":1410323,"title":"","content":"I do wonder when WW decided that Set was dead, because the feud between him and Horus continuing in Wraith would have been funny.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:19:19-07:00","id":1410324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410323#post1410323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder when WW decided that Set was dead, because the feud between him and Horus continuing in Wraith would have been funny.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Damn, i keep forgetting to make a list of &quot;dead Antediluvians to use as Neverborn&quot; in my games where Baali are broods of Caitiff haunted by them or spectres in their service. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-25-2020, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:31:19-07:00","id":1410326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410291#post1410291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know Gehenna is not canon, but I still think the section before the scenarios is interesting. The bit with the Spoiler Warning: This is the &quot;official&quot; status of the members of the Third Generation that WW kept track of and had notes on.<br /> <br /> It lists Brujah, Set, Lasombra, Ravnos, and Ventrue as having met final death.<br /> <br /> I think the most likely culprit for Set is Osiris. He had been building power for millennia, specifically vanished from Duat at the time, and hated Set since they were mortal brothers. Motive, means, opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wasn't Set like the leader of the antedilluvians in one of the scenarios?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:46:38-07:00","id":1410328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410308#post1410308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> It's a matter of taste actually. Personally there's something that i find deeply entertaining in the idea of Mithras' claim to be a childe of the Ventrue Antediluvian being as much of a lie as that of being the persian sun god. Because let's be honest, <i>how many kindred around actually have the knowledge, power and desire to challenge or prove him wrong anyway</i>? The guy was <b><i>already </i></b>a methuselah when Sejanus/Vitel was embraced, back in the early decades of the Roman Empire! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To think he came across the Assamite Antediluvian and his sense of selfworth wasn't shattered. Haqim could have easily broken his illusions about being a sun god <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> I always wondered how someone like Mithras, who has been untouchable for millennia, would act when coming face to face with someone who his two leagues above him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:50:17-07:00","id":1410331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410328#post1410328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To think he came across the Assamite Antediluvian and his sense of selfworth wasn't shattered. Haqim could have easily broken his illusions about being a sun god <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who says he <i><b>believes </b></i>that? Snake oil merchant all the way my friend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410328#post1410328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always wondered how someone like Mithras, who has been untouchable for millennia, would act when coming face to face with someone who his two leagues above him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the Path of Blood is the one group of kindred that might be actually quite ok with you diablerizing their Founder, if you can actually make it happen.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T10:51:20-07:00","id":1410332,"title":"","content":"Well given how many supernaturals can revicve even an ashed vampire id say no one is truly gone anyway.<br /> (some archmages can pull it off, some superpowerfull demons too, the Dracon kinda reincarnated all by himself and in theory guhral could also do it...they just wont for a vampire though...maybe a gurahl abomination but i kinda oubt they actually can do it anymore)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4364-orkar","name":"Orkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4364_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:57:11-07:00","id":1410403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410297#post1410297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait what was up with Veddartha and Ventrue?</div> </div> </div> </div>Veddartha was [Ventrue] until V20 authors decided that it wasn't so anymore.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T14:59:59-07:00","id":1410404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410326#post1410326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wasn't Set like the leader of the antedilluvians in one of the scenarios?</div> </div> </div> </div>After his clan had ressurected him and he ate them for their trouble.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T15:07:24-07:00","id":1410409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410308#post1410308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maltheas is some &quot;you blink &amp; you miss it&quot; Inconnu methuselah playing much younger vampire in the Council of Thorns in Transylvania Chronicles II, if memory tricks me not. More relevant for the implications he brings about Mithras than anything, truth be told.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the thing is not about &quot;much younger&quot; but more on the &quot;much younger generation&quot; issue, which specifically erases any doubt on Veddartha not being 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> - Saga<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-25T15:43:27-07:00","id":1410417,"title":"","content":"The thing is, some sources even say, that Brujah did not even died but did something similar like Saulot where he whas diablerized enough to give Troille/Tremere a 3rd generation while at the same time porting himself into the future to escape. And so it would explain why it is unable to use the timepower where you can summon a being shortly before there death from the past, because it means he really just faked his death. It would explain too, why only the True Brujah has acess to Temporis while the Brujah only have celerity. Troille made it to get the 3rd Generation but not even to use timepower beside speeding herself up which she mastered like Rock Lee mastered Taijutsu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T01:57:44-07:00","id":1410477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410308#post1410308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maltheas is some &amp;quot;you blink &amp; you miss it&amp;quot; Inconnu methuselah playing much younger vampire in the Council of Thorns in Transylvania Chronicles II, if memory tricks me not. More relevant for the implications he brings about Mithras than anything, truth be told.<br /> <br /> It's a matter of taste actually. Personally there's something that i find deeply entertaining in the idea of Mithras' claim to be a childe of the Ventrue Antediluvian being as much of a lie as that of being the persian sun god. Because let's be honest, <i>how many kindred around actually have the knowledge, power and desire to challenge or prove him wrong anyway</i>? The guy was <b><i>already </i></b>a methuselah when Sejanus/Vitel was embraced, back in the early decades of the Roman Empire! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But speaking of Antediluvians, another thing that i have done in my games overall is break from the clan-antediluvian corelation, with bits and pieces here and there implying much of the lore is imprecise or intentionally false. For example:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Among a bunch of other stuff i've thrown as &amp;quot;lore monkeywrench&amp;quot; in my chronicles. When i don't do worse, like the &amp;quot;Lucian is THE Lucian&amp;quot; or thrown some apocryphal antediluvian like i did in my rewrite of the gonzo adventure in Berlin By Night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point about Mithras lol<br /> <br /> But idc. Until there\u2019s a sourcebook that goes into detail about Veddartha not being Ventrue (more than just a throwaway reference I totally missed when I read it), I like the idea of Mithras being the childe of an Antediluvian. And maybe not even then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T05:48:26-07:00","id":1410502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410409#post1410409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the thing is not about &quot;much younger&quot; but more on the &quot;much younger generation&quot; issue, which specifically erases any doubt on Veddartha not being 3rd generation.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaannd my &quot;much younger&quot; comment related to his role impersonating a not-methuselah in Transylvania Chronicles, <b>not </b>the fact he's 5th gen while apparently having the same sire as Mithras.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410477#post1410477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good point about Mithras lol<br /> <br /> But idc. Until there\u2019s a sourcebook that goes into detail about Veddartha not being Ventrue (more than just a throwaway reference I totally missed when I read it), I like the idea of Mithras being the childe of an Antediluvian. And maybe not even then.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can understand it, the whole subject wouldn't be so divisive if not for Mithras' popularity and how many people relate see his generation and supposed origin as part of that identity. Me, i just go for that polemic bit because it adds a twist, but one that is perfectly consistent with Mithras' own portrayal.<br /> <br /> (The fact it's all about Mithras <b>actively </b>being a monumental liar tricking the whole of kindred society, instead of resting in inherited laurels of being some else's childe also appeals to me. Masquerade has more than enough NPCs trying to make themselves big through &quot;i'm the sire/childe of X&quot; and nothing else already, someone trolling this and a methuselah at that is something i can appreciate) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-26-2020, 08:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T06:03:17-07:00","id":1410504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410502#post1410502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aaaannd my &quot;much younger&quot; comment related to his role impersonating a not-methuselah in Transylvania Chronicles, <b>not </b>the fact he's 5th gen while apparently having the same sire as Mithras.</div> </div> </div> </div>When the same book has the same misinformation in stats on generation (Hardestadt as 5th, when it is widely known that the one appearing was 6th generation &quot;the Younger&quot;), it appears that the fact is that stats were of the generation they were posing as, not their true ones, therefore, Maltheas being 4th and not 5th, just like Hardestadt a paragraph away from this.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T07:13:10-07:00","id":1410509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410504#post1410504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When the same book has the same misinformation in stats on generation (Hardestadt as 5th, when it is widely known that the one appearing was 6th generation &quot;the Younger&quot;), it appears that the fact is that stats were of the generation they were posing as, not their true ones, therefore, Maltheas being 4th and not 5th, just like Hardestadt a paragraph away from this.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also the book that introduced the idea of the &quot;Younger&quot; to cover up the continuity screw-up of Harderstadt appearing in books set in periods he should have been long destroyed. Valerius, as Lady Anne's sire was supposedly 5th gen as we are introduced to her as 6th gen in A World of Darkness - until we see him as 7th in Blood &amp; Fire and are introduced to the notion of Lady Anne as a (serial) diablerist at the same time, that is.<br /> <br /> Continuity is constantly being retconned or tweaked here and there, canon exists in flux. So much the better for STs to recognize it, take everything with a grain of salt and use the pieces that better fit with their styles of play or preferences for lore/canon.<br /> <br /> You focus on some bits of canon while downplaying or ignoring others, i use some pieces in common, and some utterly unrelated ones - like ignoring Japheth/Lazarus as the Capuchin and using Constancia, that also happens to be Ambrogino's sire, instead, or using Aristotle De Laurent's reference to Critias as a major noddist in his edition of the Book of Nod's notes as an excuse to write an alternate origin myth based on the Timaeus &amp; Critias dialogues' about Atlantis, for example - and everything is perfectly fine just like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-26-2020, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T13:49:53-07:00","id":1410558,"title":"","content":"Lot of interresting stuff in this thread. Instead of quoting people, i am going to respond to some of the posts. I have had a few drinks, so take it with a grain of salt (stuck out tong emoji).<br /> <br /> About the wise and prosperous one. As for as i am concerned he is a 4th gen vampire and not an Antediluvian, and i dont even care about the Maltheas situation. The man is a member of the Inconnu. As far as i am concerned, Saulot is the head honcho of that sect. No other antedilluvian would accept being under the thumb of another. Well Maybe Absimilliard, in one story, but no other!<br /> <br /> Regardless of who the Ventrue Antedilluvian is and whatever his name is. I think we should all agree, he is still out there! Alexander, Eigerman and Antonius were made long after his supposed demise. And the beckoning is a thing! Also who the hell is Maltheas? How many lines of story does he have?<br /> <br /> About Set. I have to say i didn't know that the general consensus is: that he is dead! I figured he dissapeared like all the others. But this thread is starting to convince me of his demise. RIP, he is/was one of my favorite antes (cry emoji).<br /> <br /> About Brujah. who really cares? He has no identity at all. He might as well be dead. The story about his time jump is probably the stupidest story i have ever heard!<br /> <br /> Lasombra? How do you expect the man with instant teleportation (to the abyss) to die? He has a trump card! Isn't the story that Montana's memories were altered? That's like canon? right? Who could do that? Absimilard? He is stuck under some ice, only Lasombra was in the neighbourhood!<br /> <br /> Haqim? Well, he is the man, the myth and the legend. Did anybody other then myself even mention him? Cool dude, i like him <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-26-2020, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T14:28:32-07:00","id":1410568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410558#post1410558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lasombra? How do you expect the man with instant teleportation (to the abyss) to die? He has a trump card! Isn't the story that Montana's memories were altered? That's like canon? right? Who could do that? Absimilard? He is stuck under some ice, only Lasombra was in the neighbourhood!</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone with Dominate 3 could do that. As long as they also had the generation to affect the kindred whose minds were altered. So they would need to be of the fourth generation -or lower.<br /> <br /> I have my own speculation on what happened, but its based mostly on speculation. But in any case, I expect <i>something</i> went wrong for Lasombra.<br /> <br /> <br /> In relation to Mithras sire, London by Night quite bluntly put &quot;The Ventrue Antdiluvian&quot;. So either that is just flat out wrong, or something else is happening. And if we're going to assume something being wrong, I'd say its Maltheas entry. Its just easier to confuse a name or a generation that a flat-out Antediluvian.<br /> <br /> But things that could reconcile the discrepancy:<br /> <br /> Either &quot;Veddharta&quot; is not a unique name, but a title, or a name that has been passed on, or the name of more than one kindred. Ashur springs to mind as another Antediluvian name that seems to have multiple wearers.<br /> <br /> or more speculativly, Maltheas was sired weaker than Mithras for other reasons. The Ventrue Antediluvian has been reported to be destroyed, and to have the ability to return from final death to make its moves in the living world. Maybe it was weakened or cannot return to the world in its full potency. Tremere seems to have a similar issue.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T15:17:28-07:00","id":1410575,"title":"","content":"Really now, Trollroot, are you saying there are Ventrue going around taking the names of their sires and pretending to be them? As if THAT ever happens!<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T16:23:35-07:00","id":1410580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410568#post1410568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone with Dominate 3 could do that. As long as they also had the generation to affect the kindred whose minds were altered. So they would need to be of the fourth generation -or lower.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sure in theory, but this is Montano were are talking about. Don't think he is lacking in will power. Only a vampire with some serious juice could alter his memories. We should also consider who was there at the time. the Lasombra ante seems the most likely candidate to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24527,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","user":"blackshade","date":". 08-26-2020, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24527-blackshade","name":"blackshade","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-26T17:16:04-07:00","id":1410585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410509#post1410509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Also the book that introduced the idea of the &quot;Younger&quot; to cover up the continuity screw-up of Harderstadt appearing in books set in periods he should have been long destroyed. Valerius, as Lady Anne's sire was supposedly 5th gen as we are introduced to her as 6th gen in A World of Darkness - until we see him as 7th in Blood &amp; Fire and are introduced to the notion of Lady Anne as a (serial) diablerist at the same time, that is.<br /> <br /> Continuity is constantly being retconned or tweaked here and there, canon exists in flux. So much the better for STs to recognize it, take everything with a grain of salt and use the pieces that better fit with their styles of play or preferences for lore/canon.<br /> <br /> You focus on some bits of canon while downplaying or ignoring others, i use some pieces in common, and some utterly unrelated ones - like ignoring Japheth/Lazarus as the Capuchin and using Constancia, that also happens to be Ambrogino's sire, instead, or using Aristotle De Laurent's reference to Critias as a major noddist in his edition of the Book of Nod's notes as an excuse to write an alternate origin myth based on the Timaeus &amp; Critias dialogues' about Atlantis, for example - and everything is perfectly fine just like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing with Hardestadt was that Tyler diablerized an unnamed Ventrue elder who promoted the Camarilla (published in 1991 and then 1993 the 2nd ed). He was introduced by name in Children of the Inquisition (1992) but wasn't even mentioned in Clanbook Ventrue (1994). As he was mentioned as 5th generation (yet no single trait at 8 in neither GC1 nor GC2) perhaps dates of him in the past didn't add up and decided to create &quot;the Younger&quot; in TCII (1998) but the pieces still fit together.<br /> <br /> Anne was introduced in A World of Darkness (1992) and her character was assumed diablerist in GC2 (1996) due to the existence of Valerius being of higher generation than her. Bindusara was introduced in Clanbook Ventrue (1994) and mentioned as Valerius's sire again in GC2 (1996). Possibility of messing up by the writers, yes, but it's still fixed with no problems.<br /> <br /> Veddartha was introduced as Mithras' sire in 1992 and as 3rd generation vampire, it was considered the Ventrue Antediluvian such as Absimiliard is considered the Nosferatu's (both from the same sourcebook). If white-wolf writers messed up dates on Hardestadt, they fixed it in TC2. So if the book had some major metaplot fix, why create another one? This is the reason I believe that there is a massive misinterpretation of Maltheas not being considered the 4th generation Ventrue he was intended to appear as in TC2.<br /> <br /> I focus on what is and trying to make sense of it as thoroughly as possible but I understand that many already left that road since revised came out and simply stopped fixing things and started to give misconceptions as a way of not interfering on what was considered canonical by 2nd ed. In my games I do alter canon events at will if they suit the story but I like to keep things as is. I enjoy knowing the full lineage of every PC and understand when and why an elder might have a hand in the PCs actions, therefore, researching this helps me a lot with my stories.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T02:40:29-07:00","id":1410627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians#post1410146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are only two Antediluvians who were really destroyed, Ilyes and Zapathasura. In both cases their clans (True Brujah and Ravnos respectively) were reduced to a handful of members after their founders met Final Death. This also supports the theory that Veddartha was not really destroyed despite what the Ventrue clan elders think.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?</div> </div> </div> </div>Canon there\u2019s only ONE truly dead Antediluvian, and that\u2019s Ravnos. All the others may (or may not) have survived to present day in one form or another (even Cappadocius who became a spectre... the fact some players put it to rest is not canon per se, same with Brujah, it being killed by Troile is a legend that may or may not be true, same with Ventrue having bene killed by Brujah, and so on)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:07:37-07:00","id":1410644,"title":"","content":"Even Ravnos being truly dead is suspect because, you know, Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> I mean, White Wolf wrote themselves into a corner with the highest levels of Chimerstry involving rewriting reality at some level. It gives Ravnos an out by making people think he was taken out by the solar beam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:07:59-07:00","id":1410645,"title":"","content":"As for non canon headcanon theories in my games Brujah is not dead, Troile is a 4th generation vampire of godlike power (second city survivor) and the \u201ctrue brujah\u201d are brujah vampires who descend from those who subjected themselves to a specific ritual in Carthage. A ritual capable to alter the nature of Caine\u2019s curse. A ritual Invented (with help) by Troile Herself. The \u201ctrue\u201d part in true brujah stands for Troile belief she was able to trascend Brujah\u2019s curse elevating herself and her chosen beyond the bestial limits imposed on them by Caine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:10:38-07:00","id":1410646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410644#post1410644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Ravnos being truly dead is suspect because, you know, Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> I mean, White Wolf wrote themselves into a corner with the highest levels of Chimerstry involving rewriting reality at some level. It gives Ravnos an out by making people think he was taken out by the solar beam.</div> </div> </div> </div>We know Ravnos is dead because it was officially stated he was. Also because once he bit the dust all of his bloodline went mad","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T04:14:58-07:00","id":1410647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410646#post1410646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We know Ravnos is dead because it was officially stated he was. Also because once he bit the dust all of his bloodline went mad</div> </div> </div> </div>Ventrue and Malkav have been officially stated to be dead with evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that when Ur-shulgi broke the Tremere curse it weakened his lineage by the amount of power he required for the spell. That was a more localized usage of blood. Using 10th dot Chimerstry to rewrite reality would have been a major psychic bomb on Ravnos to pull the energy required for that.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying he's still undead, just that the possibility is there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:14:20-07:00","id":1410702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410647#post1410647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ventrue and Malkav have been officially stated to be dead with evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that when Ur-shulgi broke the Tremere curse it weakened his lineage by the amount of power he required for the spell. That was a more localized usage of blood. Using 10th dot Chimerstry to rewrite reality would have been a major psychic bomb on Ravnos to pull the energy required for that.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying he's still undead, just that the possibility is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkav, and Lasombra transcended their flesh, whatever they are, they no longer need to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce might just prove to be unkillable.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:50:44-07:00","id":1410707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410647#post1410647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ventrue and Malkav have been officially stated to be dead with evidence to the contrary.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that when Ur-shulgi broke the Tremere curse it weakened his lineage by the amount of power he required for the spell. That was a more localized usage of blood. Using 10th dot Chimerstry to rewrite reality would have been a major psychic bomb on Ravnos to pull the energy required for that.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying he's still undead, just that the possibility is there.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t remember ever reading anything like that, and there are statements on the opposite late in the revised era (Malkav resting place having been in Arcadia and him having transformed into the Madness Netwok, Ventrue having used Fortitude 10 to step out of the jhyad in order to survive gehenna).<br /> <br /> Could Chimestry 10 save Ravnos? Sure, but canonically that\u2019s not what happened. As for Ur-Shulgi \u201charming\u201d the assamite bloodline I\u2019d point you to the Assamite chapter in BJD. It explains pretty well how Ur-Shulgi broke the spell, what kind of harm befell the bloodline and why Al Asharad never tried to pull something like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 08-27-2020, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:53:15-07:00","id":1410709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackshade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410580#post1410580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sure in theory, but this is Montano were are talking about. Don't think he is lacking in will power. Only a vampire with some serious juice could alter his memories. We should also consider who was there at the time. the Lasombra ante seems the most likely candidate to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, anyone succeeding at the diableries would be high on some serious juice. People known to be there was Gratiano and the Hulul, a fourth generation Assamite. And it is interesting that the Assamites instituted ritualized diablerie of the Hulul every hundred years. Almost like they were trying to keep something from rising...<br /> <br /> And in fact, the whole &quot;people remember widely different dates etc&quot; smacks to me of someone using powers they were unfamiliar with. It seems clumsy. If you're going to cover your tracks, do it right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410702#post1410702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Malkav, and Lasombra transcended their flesh, whatever they are, they no longer need to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce might just prove to be unkillable.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Malkav and Tzimisce are on firm ground there. Lasombra less so I think. We've not heard anything to indicate that it is still in existence, and hints have gone the other way I think.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2471,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","user":"Trollroot","date":". 08-27-2020, 01:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T10:59:12-07:00","id":1410712,"title":"","content":"I like the idea as presented in Gehenna that Ventrue faked his death and is patiently waiting for the apocalypse to happen to wake up and take over as the god of the next era.<br /> <br /> But I have to say I understand why WW needs Ventrue to be dead. If Ventrue is still active, it creates one big problem: He is on-course to win the Jyhad. Because he controlls the Camarilla.<br /> Yes technically it his clan that dominates the organisation not him and not completely. But with Dominate 8 9 10. It does not matter. The clan is merely an extension of his will whether they know it or not.<br /> <br /> Now that in itself is not the real issue. The true problem is with Ventrue win-scenario being the Camarilla, he is a proponent of the status quo. A &quot;good&quot; antediluvian if you will. That is content to let his <s>slave</s> elders continue doing his bidding while he fight off his more apocalyptic minded brothers.<br /> <br /> Also Ventrue's death do solve a number of issue I have with the vampiric history. For one the weakness of clan Ventrue in the Middle East, where most of their 4th generation hail from (like most clans) and yet all the ones we know quickly settled outside the region.<br /> <br /> But without the protection of an antediluivian it makes much more sense. While Toreadors had Arikel in Mesopotamia (where she got the name), Brujah Troile in Phoenicia (from where she would later settle in the Carthaginian colony), Set in Egypt and Haquim/Cappadocius in Anatolia/Persia. They were not really in a dominant position and thus had to sought their fortunes elsewhere.<br /> It also explains why Mithras, Alexander and other Ventrues would go the such forsaken places as Paris or London after the collapse of Rome when Constantinople, Damas and Baghdad was were the cool dude were. Too much dangerous people sleeping underground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 08-27-2020, 02:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T11:08:27-07:00","id":1410714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410702#post1410702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Malkav, and Lasombra transcended their flesh, whatever they are, they no longer need to be a vampire.<br /> <br /> Tzimisce might just prove to be unkillable.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I always detested the hard on many white wolf authors had for the Tzimisce. The Eldest having infested the planet with Vicissitude was But one example of this and it just makes me remember the whole kuppaling fiasco. <br /> <br /> In my games Tzimisce and Lasombra managed to change the nature of their curse thanks to demonic aid (same with Troile but not Brujah) in order to trascend their condition and escape Caine\u2019s judgment. Ultimately they failed. Demons can help manipulate the curse but trascending it is beyond even their power because it is a \u201claw\u201d hardwired into the very nature of reality (and that\u2019s why discipline use does not cause paradox btw)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T14:21:03-07:00","id":1410761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410707#post1410707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can\u2019t remember ever reading anything like that, and there are statements on the opposite late in the revised era (Malkav resting place having been in Arcadia and him having transformed into the Madness Netwok, Ventrue having used Fortitude 10 to step out of the jhyad in order to survive gehenna).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gehenna book has Ventrue listed as long dead and the clan story is that he was killed during the time of the second city. We have evidence that he embraced after the fall of the second city (Mithras).<br /> <br /> Malkav was said to have been killed on a journey to Petra after the fall of the Second city. But the BJD has him listed as possibly being whatever it is lying in a pit in the Valley of Hinnom that is responsible for the insanity of the region.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T15:12:49-07:00","id":1410771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410714#post1410714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...example of this and it just makes me remember the whole kuppaling fiasco</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, and kudos for making word play with Kupala. None of the vampires can escape being a vampire, short of final death there is no way out. Demonic and abyssal ties just make them strange vampires.<br /> <br /> That said I am always a bit struck by interest in the Antdediluvians,as compared to how often they can be said to have a real impact on any campaign.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-27T16:47:16-07:00","id":1410779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morbus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410712#post1410712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the idea as presented in Gehenna that Ventrue faked his death and is patiently waiting for the apocalypse to happen to wake up and take over as the god of the next era.<br /> <br /> But I have to say I understand why WW needs Ventrue to be dead. If Ventrue is still active, it creates one big problem: He is on-course to win the Jyhad. Because he controlls the Camarilla.<br /> Yes technically it his clan that dominates the organisation not him and not completely. But with Dominate 8 9 10. It does not matter. The clan is merely an extension of his will whether they know it or not.<br /> <br /> Now that in itself is not the real issue. The true problem is with Ventrue win-scenario being the Camarilla, he is a proponent of the status quo. A &amp;quot;good&amp;quot; antediluvian if you will. That is content to let his <s>slave</s> elders continue doing his bidding while he fight off his more apocalyptic minded brothers.<br /> <br /> Also Ventrue's death do solve a number of issue I have with the vampiric history. For one the weakness of clan Ventrue in the Middle East, where most of their 4th generation hail from (like most clans) and yet all the ones we know quickly settled outside the region.<br /> <br /> But without the protection of an antediluivian it makes much more sense. While Toreadors had Arikel in Mesopotamia (where she got the name), Brujah Troile in Phoenicia (from where she would later settle in the Carthaginian colony), Set in Egypt and Haquim/Cappadocius in Anatolia/Persia. They were not really in a dominant position and thus had to sought their fortunes elsewhere.<br /> It also explains why Mithras, Alexander and other Ventrues would go the such forsaken places as Paris or London after the collapse of Rome when Constantinople, Damas and Baghdad was were the cool dude were. Too much dangerous people sleeping underground.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally makes sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T01:22:51-07:00","id":1410813,"title":"","content":"I think it's not entirely fair to say -Constantinople, Damas and Baghdad- were where the cool dudes were and many of the famous ancients left there out of fear of competition (Though overcrowding is certainly a cause for concern)<br /> <br /> Perhaps the vampires who moved saw the future potential in other regions. Set clearly made a good choice with Egypt, which was <i>the </i>civilization for the longest period of time. Now when it comes to moving to forsaken places like London or Paris; Perhaps that was a bit of ingenious long term planning and foresight? The rise of western european backwaters like Britain and France in the early modern period was inevitable and forseeable with an understanding of <b>geography and economics</b>, These ancients could astral project themselves to survey land and had the inhuman levels of intelligence needed to predict the future. India for example might be an incredible place with everything that it needs... but having everything that it needs keeps it somewhat complacent. The British isles were a shitty place to live where society is forced to innovate for a good standard of living; it's also an island and in an excellent spot to take advantage of that huge western continent... Given enough foresight it's not hard to believe that the have-nots of western europe will grow to conquer comfortable, resource rich lands. Mithras really picked the best possible spot for the Jyhad, and I don't think that's luck.<br /> <br /> and sure, western europe is now the comfortable, complacent land that will soon be outpaced by a rapidly modernizing Asia and eventually Africa, but the last four hundred years and how the world was globalized will be influentual forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-28-2020, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T13:30:30-07:00","id":1410874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410771#post1410771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, and kudos for making word play with Kupala. None of the vampires can escape being a vampire, short of final death there is no way out. Demonic and abyssal ties just make them strange vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are quite a few who I think tried to transcend their curse by becoming something else, but it would be perfectly on brand for the World of Darkness if the best laid plans of even these ancient monsters to escape their fates amounted to nothing in the end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T14:03:52-07:00","id":1410881,"title":"","content":"Most Antediluvians schemes seem to have some kind of transcendence as the endgame. Leaving their state and curse behind. Malkav can be said to have partially managed it, I suppose. The rest, not so much.<br /> <br /> As an asides, we are possibly in the situation where a childe of Tremere sired in the middle ages would be 4th generation, whereas one sired these days would be 5th. Tarique the Silent could also have had childer of different generations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T21:15:04-07:00","id":1410944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410881#post1410881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most Antediluvians schemes seem to have some kind of transcendence as the endgame. Leaving their state and curse behind. Malkav can be said to have partially managed it, I suppose. The rest, not so much.<br /> <br /> As an asides, we are possibly in the situation where a childe of Tremere sired in the middle ages would be 4th generation, whereas one sired these days would be 5th. Tarique the Silent could also have had childer of different generations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Tremere actually sired anyone after he achieved 3rd gen, since he was either in Torpor or fighting the worm thing/Saulot. I'm pretty sure all the rest of the council of seven got to 4th gen through Diablerie, since they started the same gen as Tremere, but I don't think any of the books specifically mentioned what gen they started with. Although all of them were made vampires in the middle ages, so you're right that 4th gen Tremere and also Giovanni as well would've been middle ages/renaissance. A lot of them could have been very old even before they were vampires, though, using magic to extend their lives. That still puts their births in the middle ages even if it's the early middle ages.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-28T22:38:43-07:00","id":1410949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410944#post1410944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Tremere actually sired anyone after he achieved 3rd gen, since he was either in Torpor or fighting the worm thing/Saulot. I'm pretty sure all the rest of the council of seven got to 4th gen through Diablerie, since they started the same gen as Tremere, but I don't think any of the books specifically mentioned what gen they started with. Although all of them were made vampires in the middle ages, so you're right that 4th gen Tremere and also Giovanni as well would've been middle ages/renaissance. A lot of them could have been very old even before they were vampires, though, using magic to extend their lives. That still puts their births in the middle ages even if it's the early middle ages.</div> </div> </div> </div>House Tremere Inner Council is believed to have all started at 5th, since all their childer are 6th. <br /> <br /> In my chronicles I established that Tremere embraced only Lucidus (HoT, pg. 137) as a failsafe since he is the only one who defeated Tremere when they were both mages.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T01:13:30-07:00","id":1410968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410761#post1410761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Malkav was said to have been killed on a journey to Petra after the fall of the Second city. But the BJD has him listed as possibly being whatever it is lying in a pit in the Valley of Hinnom that is responsible for the insanity of the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>The plot of Fountains of Bright Crimson also heavily implies this to be the case. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T03:50:26-07:00","id":1410980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrHappyAngry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410944#post1410944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Tremere actually sired anyone after he achieved 3rd gen, since he was either in Torpor or fighting the worm thing/Saulot. I'm pretty sure all the rest of the council of seven got to 4th gen through Diablerie, since they started the same gen as Tremere</div> </div> </div> </div>Grimgroth was embraced post-diablerie as a 4th generation and then raised to inner council status after goratrix left.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T08:55:42-07:00","id":1411002,"title":"","content":"There was a flaw, I think in a DA book, where a Tremere developed a nonfunctional third eye. And I think they had to be post-diablerie descendants of Tremere for it to happen.<br /> <br /> My point anyway was that there is currently a situation where an Antediluvian that has sired a fourth generation childe would now spawn fifth generation offspring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T12:59:05-07:00","id":1411018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410813#post1410813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's not entirely fair to say -Constantinople, Damas and Baghdad- were where the cool dudes were and many of the famous ancients left there out of fear of competition (Though overcrowding is certainly a cause for concern)<br /> <br /> Perhaps the vampires who moved saw the future potential in other regions. Set clearly made a good choice with Egypt, which was <i>the </i>civilization for the longest period of time. Now when it comes to moving to forsaken places like London or Paris; Perhaps that was a bit of ingenious long term planning and foresight? The rise of western european backwaters like Britain and France in the early modern period was inevitable and forseeable with an understanding of <b>geography and economics</b>, These ancients could astral project themselves to survey land and had the inhuman levels of intelligence needed to predict the future. India for example might be an incredible place with everything that it needs... but having everything that it needs keeps it somewhat complacent. The British isles were a shitty place to live where society is forced to innovate for a good standard of living; it's also an island and in an excellent spot to take advantage of that huge western continent... Given enough foresight it's not hard to believe that the have-nots of western europe will grow to conquer comfortable, resource rich lands. Mithras really picked the best possible spot for the Jyhad, and I don't think that's luck.<br /> <br /> and sure, western europe is now the comfortable, complacent land that will soon be outpaced by a rapidly modernizing Asia and eventually Africa, but the last four hundred years and how the world was globalized will be influentual forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please note that between the collapse of the Western side of the Roman Empire and &quot;the early modern period&quot;, there's a thousand years in between. Even for a Methuselah that's a long time. And that's also about the time it took for Paris to grow to a comparable size than the cities I mentioned and it will take centuries more for London to become a prize worth ruling over.<br /> <br /> For comparison that be like if a Methuselah went with the viking to the Americas in the 800's because its rise was &quot;inevitable and foreseeable with an understanding of <b>geography and economics</b>&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let's just say such decision is a bit malkavian to say the least.<br /> <br /> Also even in Western Europe they were much better cities to rule during that millennia than those two. Mostly around the Mediterranean. But again in my head cannon the reason why those Methuselah decided not to go for those better options was partly due to the rise of the Lasombra in Italy, Spain and North Africa (thanks partly to their antediluvian) but also for a desire to become the absolute ruler of their own petty kingdom after having to share for centuries at the height of the Roman Empire.<br /> <br /> It also underline an aspect of Clan Ventrue that is often underrated, and that is their pioneer and builder side. A bit like Lacroix and the guys who conquered Mexico represents as well.<br /> <br /> And sometimes, when you take risks you fail. Alexander would never see his investment bring the full benefits. Instead Paris and France became Toreadors when it became apparent that the city and the country would become the new center of Europe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24936,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","user":"Morbus","date":". 08-29-2020, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24936-morbus","name":"Morbus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-29T14:07:39-07:00","id":1411022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410980#post1410980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Grimgroth was embraced post-diablerie as a 4th generation and then raised to inner council status after goratrix left.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Source of this?<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T00:56:15-07:00","id":1411053,"title":"","content":"I don't buy that Ventrue is dead simply because the clan still has roughly the same numbers and average generation of vampires as the other clans. The Ventrue would have long since faded into a thin blooded, low population bloodline if their Ante was dead for so long.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T01:17:41-07:00","id":1411054,"title":"","content":"After the roman empire left, the city was abandoned for a short while but other places on the isles had grown at that point. Don't forget that princes claimed vast domains during this time. anglo saxons repopulated the city to 12000 in the same century. the population was 80k by 1300 which was pretty big and comfortable city back then. <br /> Also Mithras has all the Fortitude he needs to ignore english weather. <br /> I don't think it's too crazy, really. and getting an early in to the city really helps mithras to shape it how he pleases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T01:21:35-07:00","id":1411056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411022#post1411022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Source of this?<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Timeline itself was a good proof: Saulot was diablerized around 1138 and Grimgroth was embraced after the fall of Mistridge in 1204<br /> <br /> This was also confirmed in Revised by the conversation between Grimgroth and Tremere in Blood treachery<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Scene 10<br /> <br /> Two red-masked entities communicate on the Astral Plane. The first bears the distinctive mien of the FORMER TREMERE. The second remains unknown.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: What was the mat-<br /> ter, Councilor? You left Rome three years ago. Did you<br /> find these accommodations unsatisfactory also?<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: No. Nothing was unsatis-<br /> factory with the chantry.<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: Why is it, then,<br /> that I find myself holding this conversation with you?<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: We needed neither the<br /> books nor the resources. There was nothing there that<br /> could not be replaced. Indeed, we kept no resource<br /> there that we do not maintain in a dozen places besides!<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: And so you do not<br /> see the principle of the thing.<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: Principle? No, I am afraid<br /> that I am indeed blind to the \u201cprinciples\u201d behind this<br /> slaughter. I have never understood\u2014<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: And you do not<br /> understand now. Still, I am not without mercy. I am<br /> offering you a chance.<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: Your beneficence astounds<br /> me. <b>What else were you going to do? Kill me? You did<br /> that 800 years ago. I have not yet fallen down</b>.<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: You would do well<br /> to mind your tongue with me, Councilor.<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: I am not afraid anymore.<br /> Not of death. Not of you. I fear only that it is too late for<br /> me to appease the ghosts of the past and make this right.<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: Yet that is precisely<br /> what I am offering you, Councilor.<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: What do you mean?<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: You will lead an<br /> assault on the wizards\u2019 stronghold in London. Before<br /> you interrupt, let me explain. You may handle this affair<br /> in any fashion you see fit. If they surrender peacefully,<br /> you may feel free to offer them a chance to end these<br /> hostilities.<br /> <br /> FORMER TREMERE: And if they do not sur-<br /> render?<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: Then you are to take<br /> the location or destroy it. In any case, this battle will<br /> decide our stance for the remainder of this war. Con-<br /> gratulations, Councilor; you will be the only creature in<br /> history to decide the fate of the Order of Hermes twice<br /> in his lifetime. The first time, you laid it low. Mayhap<br /> this time you will raise it up from its deathly slumber.<br /> Now go.<br /> <br /> The FORMER TREMERE is dismissed, his Astral<br /> form receding from the MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE as<br /> though compelled beyond his power. A 2nd PRESENCE,<br /> veiled in the aether, steps out of Astral mists to present<br /> itself before the MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE. It\u2019s mask<br /> is similar in design.<br /> <br /> 2nd PRESENCE: Master, should we not monitor<br /> him? It is dangerous enough to give him leave to plan<br /> this matter himself.<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: No. He will attend<br /> my will in this. He has to. He believes he can end this<br /> war. Perhaps he is right. I\u2019ve no wish to waste resources<br /> on this inane conflict. His rebelliousness can be dealt<br /> with later, if at all. His honest hatred is far more valu-<br /> able to me than one soul falsely devoted for every star<br /> in the sky.<br /> <br /> 2nd PRESENCE: As you command, Master.<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: One last thing, my<br /> valued companion.<br /> <br /> 2nd PRESENCE: Yes, Master?<br /> <br /> MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: Make the prepara-<br /> tions to wake me, should all else fail.<br /> Darkness falls on the stage. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2020, 04:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T08:23:31-07:00","id":1411075,"title":"","content":"In fairness the &quot;Former Tremere&quot; is only implicitly Grimgroth, rather than being named. On a related note, in <i>Blood Treachery</i> Grimgroth dies. However, he is implied to be alive in V5 <i>Chicago by Night</i> - he send DuSable back to the Windy City after the Second Massasa War.<br /> <br /> The &quot;Mysterious Presence&quot; is supposed to be Tremere himself, but that - and all of <i>Blood Treachery</i> - does odd things to the time line. It would be interesting to make the character Saulot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T09:36:19-07:00","id":1411081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411075#post1411075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fairness the &amp;quot;Former Tremere&amp;quot; is only implicitly Grimgroth, rather than being named. On a related note, in <i>Blood Treachery</i> Grimgroth dies. However, he is implied to be alive in V5 <i>Chicago by Night</i> - he send DuSable back to the Windy City after the Second Massasa War.<br /> <br /> The &amp;quot;Mysterious Presence&amp;quot; is supposed to be Tremere himself, but that - and all of <i>Blood Treachery</i> - does odd things to the time line. It would be interesting to make the character Saulot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never read Blood Treachery. Is it worth getting? Or is it basically incompatible with the historical stuff in V20 and the timeline in V5?<br /> <br /> Anyone else can answer too \ud83d\ude0a.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:17:19-07:00","id":1411089,"title":"","content":"Grimgroth does not die in Blood Treachery. His last appearance is in page 41 and he is safe and sound.<br /> As for the implicitly...I'd say it's almost screamed. Aside from all the textual hints, you even have a portrait of Grimgroth at page 23 of Blood Treachery, which is a modified version of the Grimgroth portrait in Clanbook Tremere 2nd ed p.64<br /> <br /> <br /> Clanbook Tremere portrait of Grimgroth<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/7/7f/Grimgroth.gif/revision/latest/top-crop/width/360/height/450?cb=20140423163921\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> and...Blood Treachery<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.ibb.co/4TXPGyT/Grimgr.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <br /> Aside from that, the Mage line later confirmed that it was Grimgroth.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the book itself is very good*, and it has a very interesting format (a theater piece). That said it is very Order of Hermes - Tremere specific, so it's worth having only in a Tremere focused perspective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> * Even so some fan of Mage do not like for several reason, most of important the fact that the Order of Hermes doesn't do a great perfomance in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2020, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:35:04-07:00","id":1411093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410980#post1410980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Grimgroth was embraced post-diablerie as a 4th generation and then raised to inner council status after goratrix left.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's neat, I didn't realize any of the council were post saulot diablerie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14519-drhappyangry","name":"DrHappyAngry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14519_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:43:13-07:00","id":1411094,"title":"","content":"He is the only one confirmed, and he is also a very special one. I doubt that any other Councilor would have the gall to spit in Tremere face. Goratrix chose to flee rather than face his wrath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2020, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T10:55:55-07:00","id":1411100,"title":"","content":"As I noted in another thread, I don't buy that [Ventrue] was killed right outside the Second City. There are too many relatively young Ventrue of 4th generation wandering about for me to believe they all drank their way up the ladder. Alexander and Erik come to mind.<br /> <br /> Also, it would be kinda hilarious to me if there isn't an actual Jyhad between the Founders. They wake up now and again, look after their favourite childer, explore the world a bit, and go back to sleep and/or try to transcend their vampiric state some more. For all we know, [Ventrue] is just one of the few not into all the mystical mumbo-jumbo her peers get into and she's perfectly content exploring the new and exciting ways in which the planet changed since her last visit.<br /> <br /> Regarding Blood Treachery, it's an interesting read. Very different from the norm. I liked it, but I also used to act with several amateur theatre projects in the past. However, yes, the Order does get a very bad rep in it. And the part with the Tremere Founder is confusing, because he plays himself up as being TREMERE, not Saulot-as-Tremere, when there isn't a single Tremere present he'd have to fool.<br /> <br /> Makes one wonder if Tremere (in the original body) is actually a mix of both Saulot and he, and the other one (in Goratrix's body) is ALSO a mix between them. Now that would be a cluster fook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T11:07:37-07:00","id":1411103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411100#post1411100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I noted in another thread, I don't buy that [Ventrue] was killed right outside the Second City. There are too many relatively young Ventrue of 4th generation wandering about for me to believe they all drank their way up the ladder. Alexander and Erik come to mind.<br /> <br /> Also, it would be kinda hilarious to me if there isn't an actual Jyhad between the Founders. They wake up now and again, look after their favourite childer, explore the world a bit, and go back to sleep and/or try to transcend their vampiric state some more. For all we know, [Ventrue] is just one of the few not into all the mystical mumbo-jumbo her peers get into and she's perfectly content exploring the new and exciting ways in which the planet changed since her last visit.<br /> <br /> Regarding Blood Treachery, it's an interesting read. Very different from the norm. I liked it, but I also used to act with several amateur theatre projects in the past. However, yes, the Order does get a very bad rep in it. And the part with the Tremere Founder is confusing, because he plays himself up as being TREMERE, not Saulot-as-Tremere, when there isn't a single Tremere present he'd have to fool.<br /> <br /> Makes one wonder if Tremere (in the original body) is actually a mix of both Saulot and he, and the other one (in Goratrix's body) is ALSO a mix between them. Now that would be a cluster fook.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As for Ventrue there are WAY to many young Ventrues. Alexander, Eigermann and Antonius must have been embraced in the first millenium B.C.<br /> The other also seems &quot;younger&quot;. Mithras (if he was embraced by Ventrue) was embraced in 1200 b.c., and I doubt that Tinia among the Etruscans could be too old, the Eutruscans started their history around 900 b.c..<br /> <br /> By the way it does seems that there is some kind of road map, the oldest members of the Ventrue clan hail from the Eeast and Sumer (Arakur, Orthia, Nefer-Meri-Isis, Mithras), then we have Alexander in 700 b.c. in Greece and Tinia in Etruria, and last we have Antiorix and Eigerman among the celts and the germans (oldest celtic culture is the Hallstat culture, 800-450 b.c.).<br /> So it seems that Ventrue moved from Sumer to the western mediterrean, and from there he pushed north to the Celts, who were well known by the Greeks (as the Galatians) and by the Etruscans who lived near them.<br /> <br /> It should be noted that in Blood Treachery Tremere tells to Etrius &quot;MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE: Make the preparations<br /> to wake me, should all else fail.&quot;<br /> <br /> Which sounds like there are magical things to do to make Tremere operative (he meet Grimgroth in the Astral Plane, non face to face in real world), and also it sounds like awakening is some kind of last resort, and to be attempted only if everything else fail.<br /> So in Blood Treachery Tremere would prefer not to be awakened, and even so awakening him requires some work from Etrius","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2020, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T11:17:54-07:00","id":1411105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411081#post1411081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I never read Blood Treachery. Is it worth getting? Or is it basically incompatible with the historical stuff in V20 and the timeline in V5?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is... different. The book is written in the format of a play, breaking down sections into Acts (Act I, Act II, ect) and it handles the heavy exposition by having NPCs talk to each other. There is a lot of PCs to do, but it is still a plot heavily and even railroaded story, just one with a different format.<br /> <br /> It is not incompatible, at least no more so than some other books. In terms of strict adherence to the supposed timeline, Blood Treachery poses the question of when Tremere left his body to Saulot and moved into the body of Goratrix. In this book Tremere does not seem to contend with Saulot at all, and has the power and time to deal with the war with the wizards. Other books suggest some time after this point Tremere moved into the body of Goratrix. Yet others suggest that happened back in the middle ages.<br /> <br /> In any case, I would say the book is an interesting work, with useful material, but one that does not stick the landing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411089#post1411089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Grimgroth does not die in Blood Treachery. His last appearance is in page 41 and he is safe and sound.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has been years since I read the book, but I thought the final scene had Grimgroth captured by the Hermetics, only for Tremere to channel himself through Grimgroths body (and call the wizards a bunch of dweebs and make the shape of an L on his foreheard) and then Grimgroths body burst into flames when the spirit of Tremere left.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T11:22:49-07:00","id":1411106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411105#post1411105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It has been years since I read the book, but I thought the final scene had Grimgroth captured by the Hermetics, only for Tremere to channel himself through Grimgroths body (and call the wizards a bunch of dweebs and make the shape of an L on his foreheard) and then Grimgroths body burst into flames when the spirit of Tremere left.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's not Grimgroth, Tremere possess Master Cordevera, of the House Tytalus, who has ingested Tremere blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Pause.<br /> Before he can say more, CORDOVERA\u2019s eyes spout<br /> fountains of blood. He screams. Guards rush to help, but<br /> bolts of electricity shoot from his body, stunning them.<br /> CORDOVERA\u2019s face begins twitching, and his clothes begin<br /> changing. A massive telekinetic wave sends every mage<br /> sprawling. CORDOVERA\u2019s hands erupt into flame. And<br /> then, suddenly, it is no longer CORDOVERA, but a figure<br /> that wears the blood-red mask of a VAMPIRE ANCIENT.<br /> The masked figure, a spirit projected through undead powers<br /> into the very heart of the Traditions, radiates authority that<br /> will not be questioned. The mask bears a striking resemblance<br /> to that of the MYSTERIOUS PRESENCE in Act<br /> Two, Scene 10.<br /> The assembled magi stand, stunned. One FLAMBEAU<br /> rushes toward the ANCIENT. The mask turns to face the<br /> FLAMBEAU, and the FLAMBEAU is frozen in place.<br /> No one else dares to move.<br /> ANCIENT: No welcome for the prodigal son, then?<br /> More\u2019s the pity, I suppose. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T12:02:25-07:00","id":1411108,"title":"","content":"So some thoughts:<br /> <br /> The OG Antes deliberately tried to sire opposing clans with varied skills in order to have all-encompassing control. You know how there are five companies controlling 90% of USA media and they make products with a controlled diversity of opinion so the average person is tricked into thinking that their opinion matters and that there are people on their side and opponents and it's not all just an oligarch's theatre? yeah it's like that.<br /> <br /> Broad spectrum Antes:<br /> Ventrue made Brujah.<br /> Toreador made the Nosferatu.<br /> Saulot made the Baali. Could have made the malkavians. (of course, Malkav could have made Saulot and the Malkavians... it doesn't really matter. This is true for everything else IE Nosferatu made the Toreador...)<br /> Enoia made a lot of things, Set being one of them.<br /> <br /> One true way antes:<br /> Tzmisce: I do wonder if he's Haquim<br /> Ravnos: Happy with his chimestry.<br /> Lasombra: made a number of african bloodlines<br /> Capadocious... A lot of his bloodlines are known, I don't need to explain them.<br /> <br /> Of course, I'm open to unexpected combinations. <br /> First one to slay god wins. Maybe they're working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T14:15:32-07:00","id":1411119,"title":"","content":"On Ventrue, I find this entry on Hardestadt the Mysterious to be rather interesting. One interpretation of Hardestadt's name could be &quot;placeholder of many&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/User_blog:Ryanchaddock/Hardestadt_the_Mysterious\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Us...the_Mysterious</a><br /> <br /> Did Tyler truly diablerize Hardestadt? Perhaps it was a ruse and Hardestadt The Elder faked his death (he certainly wouldn't be the first to do this). Hardestadt may have very well dominated Tyler and any others present, altering their memories of the incident, and handed over a newly embraced pawn for Tyler to diablerize while dominated, all to make the death of Hardestadt The Elder more believable.<br /> <br /> Also, sometime after 1222 CE, Alexander of Paris at one point went to Hardestadt The Elder and requested asylum. I find it strange that Alexander, a vampire just shy of 2000 years old, would seek out help from Hardestadt The Elder, who was about 275 years old at the time.<br /> <br /> Hardestadt's heraldic motto was Vincam etiam ab inferis (&quot;Even From The Grave I Shall Conquer&quot;).<br /> <br /> I think Hardestadt The Elder faked his death. Moreover, supposedly on the last night before the Deluge destroyed the First City, Caine visited [Ventrue] and entrusted him with the role of caretaker of all of Caine's descendants. Without arguing the Camarilla's merits, I could see a character such as Ventrue viewing the creation of the Camarilla as a way to safeguard Cainites. Hardestadt The Elder, &quot;placeholder of many&quot;, could indeed be Ventrue, who has faked his death and taken on different identities multiple times throughout history.<br /> <br /> Yes, Hardestadt The Elder's generation was listed as 5th, but can you truly take that, or many of the other things in the World of Darkness, at face value? Writers lie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-30T15:35:32-07:00","id":1411127,"title":"","content":"I tend do agree that Hardestadt story is far more complex than what it seems. I also subscribe the theory about Hardestadt faking his death. I always tought that his motto was...quite meaningfull.<br /> <br /> Another theory I have is that Hardestadt might be the childe of Antonius.<br /> In Dark Age Ventrue Novel, Jurgen says that his sire might be as old as Julia Antasia (480 b.c.)<br /> Bavaria, where Hardestadt was embraced, was Gaul's lands once*, and the Gauls were ruled by Antiorix. Even more it is said in Dark Age 20th companion that the faction of Ventrue led by Julia Antasia is at war with the heirs of Antonius, and yet Antasians never had a stake in Costantinople's history. Their main enemy is the Ventrue faction lead by Hardestadt. At the same time Antonius shared many things with Hardestatdt. The enforcement of the Masquerade in Byzantium was among the strictest in the middle age, just like in the Black Fiefs of Hardestadt, and the Iconoclast campaing led by Antonius against Cainite mysticism was very akin to the persecution of Noddism made by Hardestadt.<br /> Even more...it would give a new meaning to the feud between Hardestadt and Vykos.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Funny thing, Hardestadt was embraced in Bavaria, and Bavaria is the home of the Hallstadt culture, the oldest Celtic culture we know about.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallstatt_culture#:~:text=The%20Hallstatt%20culture%20was%20the,12th%20century%20BC%20(Late%20Bronze\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallst...(Late%20Bronze</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 08-30-2020, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T08:17:14-07:00","id":1411644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1410585#post1410585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Veddartha was introduced as Mithras' sire in 1992 and as 3rd generation vampire, it was considered the Ventrue Antediluvian such as Absimiliard is considered the Nosferatu's (both from the same sourcebook). If white-wolf writers messed up dates on Hardestadt, they fixed it in TC2. So if the book had some major metaplot fix, why create another one? This is the reason I believe that there is a massive misinterpretation of Maltheas not being considered the 4th generation Ventrue he was intended to appear as in TC2.<br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if this has been pointed out before but Veddartha has a third childe, older than the others. Balthazar. Fought the Baali centuries before Mithras was embraced. Sire of Anushin Rawan and Ea Adapa. Anyone got a generation on any of them?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T10:32:38-07:00","id":1411651,"title":"","content":"I blame the True Brujah for these timeline issues. Well, them, their Great race of Yith masters and the Time War in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-03T20:27:07-07:00","id":1411740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411644#post1411644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forgive me if this has been pointed out before but Veddartha has a third childe, older than the others. Balthazar. Fought the Baali centuries before Mithras was embraced. Sire of Anushin Rawan and Ea Adapa. Anyone got a generation on any of them?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Balthazar appeared in only two sources, Dark Ages Companion and Encyclopaedia Vampirica (semi-canon since it was translated from the german Vampire line by Feder und Schwert). He is a childe of [Ventrue] and most probably the eldest of them all, it's a shame he wasn't mentioned in the retconned of the other 4th generation Ventrue of DA Companion V20. Before this revision, the original childer were Balthazar, Medon, Mithras, Alexander and Antonius.<br /> <br /> Both Anushin Rawan and Ea Adapa has to be considered 5th generation and most probably contemporaries of Arakur and Tiamat.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:01:48-07:00","id":1411784,"title":"","content":"Is there a huge difference between a 4th Gen who\u2019s maybe three or four thousand years old and one who\u2019s a lot older? (Tiamat has to be at least 3000 years old if she\u2019s the vampire the Babylonian goddess Tiamat is based on.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T07:09:10-07:00","id":1411788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411784#post1411784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a huge difference between a 4th Gen who\u2019s maybe three or four thousand years old and one who\u2019s a lot older? (Tiamat has to be at least 3000 years old if she\u2019s the vampire the Babylonian goddess Tiamat is based on.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Tiamat is AT LEAST 6000 years old, her profile is in Diablerize London","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T10:34:05-07:00","id":1411830,"title":"","content":"Then she\u2019s almost unimaginably old. Way older than Babylon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:00:28-07:00","id":1411835,"title":"","content":"Actually Tiamat is more likely to be between 4000 and 4200 years old given that in her backstory its mentioned that she was taken to the ziggarut of ur prior to her embrace, which is believe to have been built in the 21st century BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26129-harbinger1999","name":"Harbinger1999","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26129_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T11:58:07-07:00","id":1411846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Harbinger1999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411835#post1411835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Tiamat is more likely to be between 4000 and 4200 years old given that in her backstory its mentioned that she was taken to the ziggarut of ur prior to her embrace, which is believe to have been built in the 21st century BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes more sense. That\u2019s about when the Babylonian civilization started.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:10:37-07:00","id":1411849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Harbinger1999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411835#post1411835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Tiamat is more likely to be between 4000 and 4200 years old given that in her backstory its mentioned that she was taken to the ziggarut of ur prior to her embrace, which is believe to have been built in the 21st century BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want the history of the WoD to match the history of the real world then the dates of the embraces of a lot of 4th gens make little to no sense. Fortunately the WoD is a fictional universe so you can easily change things to make sense. For example what if the deluge really was the moment reality started to coalesce in its current form after the end of the war between demons and angels? What if time was &quot;malleable&quot; for a period and it stretched back and forth for a while making it possible for a lot of things to happen that make no sense for &quot;official history&quot;?<br /> <br /> That's how I dealt with the inconstincencies in the timeline of several WoD games making them work together. The only other option is to just adapt everything to real world history but I feel like it's a lot of effort for little to no payback and it's something that even diminishes the possibilities for fun in a chronicle devoted to uncover the secret history of the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24992,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","user":"Haquim","date":". 09-04-2020, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:23:16-07:00","id":1411853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411784#post1411784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a huge difference between a 4th Gen who\u2019s maybe three or four thousand years old and one who\u2019s a lot older? (Tiamat has to be at least 3000 years old if she\u2019s the vampire the Babylonian goddess Tiamat is based on.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Overall experience and discipline sets, mostly. Montano and Gratiano are separated by a couple thousand years and there are things that Montano can do with Obtenebration that Gratiano cannot due to the age gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T12:46:49-07:00","id":1411858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411784#post1411784\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a huge difference between a 4th Gen who\u2019s maybe three or four thousand years old and one who\u2019s a lot older? (Tiamat has to be at least 3000 years old if she\u2019s the vampire the Babylonian goddess Tiamat is based on.)</div> </div> </div> </div>As a general rule, yes. The older the vampire the more powerful it is. That said, not all vampires are created equal, some are simply more skilled, intelligent, adaptable than others. Take ur-Shulgi, one of the most powerful 4th generation vampires ever presented. It's clearly stated his embrace was special and on top of that he is a second city vampire which means he's unfathomably old.<br /> <br /> On the other hand you may have vampires like Critias, a 5th gen methuselah whose stats are clearly mediocre, which can only be justified in game with the idea he did not spend a lot of time trying to improve himself, as the unlifestyle of any vampires will influence their abilities and power level. It doesn't matter if you are 3 thousand years old when you spent them playing chess or in torpor.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:31:54-07:00","id":1411868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Harbinger1999</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411835#post1411835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Tiamat is more likely to be between 4000 and 4200 years old given that in her backstory its mentioned that she was taken to the ziggarut of ur prior to her embrace, which is believe to have been built in the 21st century BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>The WoD has always been contradictory when it comes to reconciling real history with historical mentions in its games. Often this is because the writer simply didn't know any better and was incorrect when depicting history. But sometimes this is probably a result of history in the WoD simply being different. While I think historical accuracy should be attempted in most cases, I am much more willing to accept divergences in the ancient past (which is much less documented and more unknown) than more recent eras.<br /> <br /> In the instance of Tiamat and other extremely ancient Methusalehs, I'm more willing to go with the way it was originally written than try to change things retroactively to fit history as we know it now. The more important thing about Tiamat is her very ancient origins than the actual time when the ziggurat was built. Besides, it's easy to say that there was some other temple or building being used than the actual ziggurat if that is really crucial to someone. But I also think it's cool to say that the ziggurat of Ur was in fact in existence at the time in the WoD, and that human archaeologists either got it wrong, or that in the WoD they've confirmed it was built thousands of years earlier (which is true in that world, if not our own).<br /> <br /> While I do think historical mentions should be made as accurate as possible, in the end the WoD's history is only inspired by real history, not the real thing. Some fudging is allowed provided it fits good Gothic tropes (and preferably with it being mentioned that things were different so it doesn't confuse anyone, or cause a negative reaction by people who do know).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-04T13:53:00-07:00","id":1411878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1410146-destroyed-antediluvians?p=1411868#post1411868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The WoD has always been contradictory when it comes to reconciling real history with historical mentions in its games. Often this is because the writer simply didn't know any better and was incorrect when depicting history. But sometimes this is probably a result of history in the WoD simply being different. While I think historical accuracy should be attempted in most cases, I am much more willing to accept divergences in the ancient past (which is much less documented and more unknown) than more recent eras.<br /> <br /> In the instance of Tiamat and other extremely ancient Methusalehs, I'm more willing to go with the way it was originally written than try to change things retroactively to fit history as we know it now. The more important thing about Tiamat is her very ancient origins than the actual time when the ziggurat was built. Besides, it's easy to say that there was some other temple or building being used than the actual ziggurat if that is really crucial to someone. But I also think it's cool to say that the ziggurat of Ur was in fact in existence at the time in the WoD, and that human archaeologists either got it wrong, or that in the WoD they've confirmed it was built thousands of years earlier (which is true in that world, if not our own).<br /> <br /> While I do think historical mentions should be made as accurate as possible, in the end the WoD's history is only inspired by real history, not the real thing. Some fudging is allowed provided it fits good Gothic tropes (and preferably with it being mentioned that things were different so it doesn't confuse anyone, or cause a negative reaction by people who do know).</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you. In historical romances history always comes second to romance, and Gothic literature is descended from and inspired by romance novels. It\u2019s great when history clicks perfectly with your game; when it doesn\u2019t, you fix the history a little.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}